From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] local: soc: qcom: aoss: keep X1E out of AOSD at EL2

With Linux at EL2 the SoC hard-resets (PS_HOLD, Hard Reset) whenever an
hourly firmware event, counted from boot, finds it in AOSD (XO shutdown).
Every s2idle reset on the Yoga Slim 7x lands at boot + N h + 48-50 s,
including sleeps only 15 and 32 minutes old, and the Vivobook S15 shows
the same pattern. CXSD and DDR low-power mode are not affected.

Ask AOP for CXSD only, as the x1e-sleep project does with an out-of-tree
module: {class: aoss_slp, res: sleep, val: disable}. Measured on the Yoga:
without it, s2idle enters AOSD within seconds; with it, s2idle stays in
CXSD/DDR LPM for ~99% of the sleep (202 mW on battery) and sleeps through
the reset point.

Limited to x1e80100 booted at EL2, where it was observed. The debugfs
prevent_aoss_sleep knob cannot do this: its message has no val key.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/mailbox_client.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_platform.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/thermal.h>
@@ -15,6 +16,8 @@
 #include <linux/string_choices.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.h>
 
+#include <asm/virt.h>
+
 #define CREATE_TRACE_POINTS
 #include "trace-aoss.h"
 
@@ -623,6 +626,14 @@
 
 	qmp_debugfs_create(qmp);
 
+	/* local: an hourly firmware event resets X1E at EL2 if it lands in AOSD */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,x1e80100") && is_hyp_mode_available()) {
+		if (qmp_send(qmp, "{class: aoss_slp, res: sleep, val: disable}"))
+			dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "failed to disable AOSD\n");
+		else
+			dev_info(&pdev->dev, "AOSD disabled, system sleep stops at CXSD\n");
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 
 err_close_qmp:
